    "title": "Is the 'Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special' out? How to stream",
    "text": "Updated March 23, 2026, 2:02 p.m. ETMiley Cyrus and Disney have released a special to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the Disney Channel show \"Hannah Montana.\"The \"Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special\" is now available to stream exclusively on Disney+.The special features an interview with Cyrus, archival footage, and performances of songs from the show.Happy \"Hannahversary\" to all who celebrate!Miley Cyrus, along with Disney, is releasing its highly anticipated 20th-anniversary special for Disney Channel's hit teen sitcom \"Hannah Montana\" early tomorrow.The singer, 33, honors the iconic fictional superstar during the Disney+ special, which she portrayed from 2006 to 2011. The special promises to be a nostalgic look back at the show's music and major moments.\"'Hannah Montana' will always be a part of who I am,\" Cyrus said in a statement earlier this year. \"What started as a TV show became a shared experience that shaped my life and the lives of so many fans, and I'll always be thankful for that connection. The fact that it still means so much to people all these years later is something I'm very proud of. This 'Hannahversary' is my way of celebrating and thanking the fans who've stood by me for 20 years.\"Watch the trailer for the 'Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special'When is the 'Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special?' How to streamThe \"Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special\" will be available to stream on Disney+ on March 24 at 3 a.m. ET.Watch 'Hannah Montana' anniversary special on Disney+What is the 'Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special?'According to USA TODAY, the special is filmed in front of a live studio audience and features an interview with Cyrus conducted by \"Call Her Daddy\" host Alex Cooper, in which the singer will reflect on the series' creation and impact.There will be never-before-seen archival footage, and some of the show's most memorable sets will be \"brought back to life — including the Stewart family living room and the legendary Hannah Montana closet,\" Disney said. \"There will also be some familiar notes that find their way back into the spotlight,\" the announcement teased.Cyrus also performed some of her hit songs from the show: This Is the Life,” “The Climb,” and “The Best of Both Worlds.” According to Variety, she also has a new, original song that will appear in the special.When did Disney Channel's 'Hannah Montana' end?Cyrus rose to fame from her starring role on \"Hannah Montana,\" which aired on Disney Channel from March 24, 2006, until Jan. 16, 2011, according to IMDb.The 100-episode series starred Cyrus alongside Emily Osment, Mitchel Musso and her actual father, country singer Billy Ray Cyrus. Two \"Hannah Montana\" movies were also created and released by Disney.The \"Hannah Montana\" character had five studio albums, according to Genius.When did Miley Cyrus last tour as Hannah Montana? Did she go to Florida?The last time Miley Cyrus performed as Hannah Montana was in 2008 on the \"Best of Both Worlds Tour,\" according to Songkick.The tour promoted her double-disc album \"Hannah Montana 2: Meet Miley Cyrus\" and showcased Cyrus's first-ever concerts as herself. The tour was considered \"highly successful,\" selling out multiple shows and grossing over $54 million.Cyrus performed sold-out concerts in four Florida cities: Tampa, Miami, Jacksonville and Orlando.Is Miley Cyrus touring again as Hannah Montana?Despite early internet rumors that Cyrus would hit the road again as her persona, no plans have been announced for a new \"Hannah Montana\" tour.However, USA TODAY notes a tour might be unlikely.During a May 2023 interview with British Vogue, Cyrus — whose last world tour was the 2014 Bangerz Tour — said she had no desire to go on tour. The \"Something Beautiful\" singer added that while she enjoys performing for her friends, \"singing for hundreds of thousands of people isn't really the thing that I love.\"\"There's no connection. There's no safety,\" Cyrus explained. \"It's also not natural. It's so isolating because if you're in front of 100,000 people, then you are alone.\"Watch episodes of 'Hannah Montana' ahead of the anniversaryFor those wanting to binge the series again before the special, you can find all four seasons on Disney+, FuboTV and YouTube TV.Watch 'Hannah Montana' on Disney+You can also purchase episodes on Apple TV.Relive 'Best of Both Worlds' tour: Where to stream Hannah Montana concert movieWhether you were lucky enough to attend Cyrus's tours as Hannah Montana or instead experienced your first heartbreak over not getting tickets, you can still relive the magic of the \"Best of Both Worlds\" tour.The \"Hannah Montana & Miley Cyrus: Best of Both Worlds Concert\" movie is available to stream on Disney+. Watch 'Hannah Montana' tour movie on Disney+You can also rent or purchase it on platforms such as Roku, Prime Video, Apple TV, and Fandango at Home.Contributing: Brendan Morrow, USA TODAYSamantha Neely is a trending reporter for the USA TODAY NETWORK-Florida, covering pop culture, theme parks, breaking news and more. You can get all of Florida’s best content directly in your inbox each weekday by signing up for the free newsletter, Florida TODAY, at https://floridatoday.com/newsletters.",
